{"id":"sample_b2-nasa-sciencecasts","videoId":"B1UQHhZHeiA","title":"ScienceCasts: Planetary Defense","author":"NASA Science","videoDuration":319000,"lang":"en","transcriptHash":"430df8c748763030968679137ea7ddcd","source":"supadata","start":23820,"end":159360,"sentences":[{"id":"s0_23820","text":"When an asteroid targeted Earth 65 million years ago, it took those masters of Earth by complete surprise.","words":[{"w":"When","start":23820,"end":24140},{"w":"an","start":24140,"end":24332},{"w":"asteroid","start":24332,"end":24908},{"w":"targeted","start":24908,"end":25484},{"w":"Earth","start":25484,"end":25869},{"w":"65","start":25869,"end":26061},{"w":"million","start":26061,"end":26573},{"w":"years","start":26573,"end":26957},{"w":"ago,","start":26957,"end":27277},{"w":"it","start":27277,"end":27469},{"w":"took","start":27469,"end":27789},{"w":"those","start":27789,"end":28173},{"w":"masters","start":28173,"end":28685},{"w":"of","start":28685,"end":28877},{"w":"Earth","start":28877,"end":29262},{"w":"by","start":29262,"end":29454},{"w":"complete","start":29454,"end":30030},{"w":"surprise.","start":30030,"end":30670}],"start":23820,"end":30670,"timing":"line","chunks":[0,3,5,9,15],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"6500万年前、地球に向かって飛んできた小惑星は、地球の支配者たちを完全に驚かせた。","edge":false,"segFrom":4,"segTo":4},{"id":"s1_30690","text":"While we know of no large object that is on a collision course with Earth in the next 100 years,","words":[{"w":"While","start":30690,"end":31011},{"w":"we","start":31011,"end":31172},{"w":"know","start":31172,"end":31439},{"w":"of","start":31439,"end":31600},{"w":"no","start":31600,"end":31760},{"w":"large","start":31760,"end":32081},{"w":"object","start":32081,"end":32456},{"w":"that","start":32456,"end":32723},{"w":"is","start":32723,"end":32884},{"w":"on","start":32884,"end":33044},{"w":"a","start":33044,"end":33151},{"w":"collision","start":33151,"end":33686},{"w":"course","start":33686,"end":34061},{"w":"with","start":34061,"end":34328},{"w":"Earth","start":34328,"end":34649},{"w":"in","start":34649,"end":34810},{"w":"the","start":34810,"end":35024},{"w":"next","start":35024,"end":35291},{"w":"100","start":35291,"end":35505},{"w":"years,","start":35505,"end":35880}],"start":30690,"end":35880,"timing":"line","chunks":[0,7,15],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"次の100年間に地球に衝突する大きな物体はないと知られているが、","edge":false,"segFrom":5,"segTo":5},{"id":"s2_35900","text":"descendants of survivors from that catastrophic impact are determined not to make the same mistake.","words":[{"w":"descendants","start":35900,"end":36705},{"w":"of","start":36705,"end":36907},{"w":"survivors","start":36907,"end":37578},{"w":"from","start":37578,"end":37913},{"w":"that","start":37913,"end":38249},{"w":"catastrophic","start":38249,"end":39121},{"w":"impact","start":39121,"end":39591},{"w":"are","start":39591,"end":39859},{"w":"determined","start":39859,"end":40597},{"w":"not","start":40597,"end":40865},{"w":"to","start":40865,"end":41067},{"w":"make","start":41067,"end":41402},{"w":"the","start":41402,"end":41671},{"w":"same","start":41671,"end":42006},{"w":"mistake.","start":42006,"end":42610}],"start":35900,"end":42610,"timing":"line","chunks":[0,3,7,9],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"その大惨事の生存者の子孫たちは、同じ過ちを繰り返さないと決意している。","edge":false,"segFrom":6,"segTo":6},{"id":"s3_42630","text":"In 2016, human astronomers now routinely scan the heavens for signs of potentially hazardous objects.","words":[{"w":"In","start":42630,"end":42838},{"w":"2016,","start":42838,"end":43253},{"w":"human","start":43253,"end":43668},{"w":"astronomers","start":43668,"end":44499},{"w":"now","start":44499,"end":44776},{"w":"routinely","start":44776,"end":45468},{"w":"scan","start":45468,"end":45814},{"w":"the","start":45814,"end":46091},{"w":"heavens","start":46091,"end":46645},{"w":"for","start":46645,"end":46921},{"w":"signs","start":46921,"end":47337},{"w":"of","start":47337,"end":47544},{"w":"potentially","start":47544,"end":48375},{"w":"hazardous","start":48375,"end":49067},{"w":"objects.","start":49067,"end":49690}],"start":42630,"end":49690,"timing":"line","chunks":[0,2,4,9],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"2016年、人間の天文学者たちは、今や定期的に天空を、潜在的に危険な物体の兆候を探している。","edge":false,"segFrom":7,"segTo":7},{"id":"s4_49710","text":"When one is discovered, alerts are issued to observers around the world so space rocks cannot easily disappear into the blackness of space.","words":[{"w":"When","start":49710,"end":50016},{"w":"one","start":50016,"end":50260},{"w":"is","start":50260,"end":50444},{"w":"discovered,","start":50444,"end":51177},{"w":"alerts","start":51177,"end":51605},{"w":"are","start":51605,"end":51850},{"w":"issued","start":51850,"end":52278},{"w":"to","start":52278,"end":52461},{"w":"observers","start":52461,"end":53073},{"w":"around","start":53073,"end":53501},{"w":"the","start":53501,"end":53745},{"w":"world","start":53745,"end":54112},{"w":"so","start":54112,"end":54296},{"w":"space","start":54296,"end":54663},{"w":"rocks","start":54663,"end":55029},{"w":"cannot","start":55029,"end":55457},{"w":"easily","start":55457,"end":55885},{"w":"disappear","start":55885,"end":56497},{"w":"into","start":56497,"end":56803},{"w":"the","start":56803,"end":57047},{"w":"blackness","start":57047,"end":57659},{"w":"of","start":57659,"end":57842},{"w":"space.","start":57842,"end":58270}],"start":49710,"end":58270,"timing":"line","chunks":[0,4,7,12,15,18],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"一つが発見されると、世界中の観測者に警告が出されるので、宇宙の岩が宇宙の暗黒に簡単に消えないようにする。","edge":false,"segFrom":8,"segTo":8},{"id":"s5_58290","text":"NASA-funded survey projects have found 98 percent of the known catalogue of almost 15,000 near-Earth objects-asteroids and comets whose orbits periodically bring them within 30 million miles of Earth's orbit.","words":[{"w":"NASA-funded","start":58290,"end":58995},{"w":"survey","start":58995,"end":59407},{"w":"projects","start":59407,"end":59936},{"w":"have","start":59936,"end":60229},{"w":"found","start":60229,"end":60582},{"w":"98","start":60582,"end":60758},{"w":"percent","start":60758,"end":61228},{"w":"of","start":61228,"end":61405},{"w":"the","start":61405,"end":61640},{"w":"known","start":61640,"end":61992},{"w":"catalogue","start":61992,"end":62580},{"w":"of","start":62580,"end":62756},{"w":"almost","start":62756,"end":63168},{"w":"15,000","start":63168,"end":63579},{"w":"near-Earth","start":63579,"end":64226},{"w":"objects-asteroids","start":64226,"end":65284},{"w":"and","start":65284,"end":65519},{"w":"comets","start":65519,"end":65930},{"w":"whose","start":66950,"end":67360},{"w":"orbits","start":67360,"end":67838},{"w":"periodically","start":67838,"end":68725},{"w":"bring","start":68725,"end":69135},{"w":"them","start":69135,"end":69476},{"w":"within","start":69476,"end":69954},{"w":"30","start":69954,"end":70159},{"w":"million","start":70159,"end":70706},{"w":"miles","start":70706,"end":71115},{"w":"of","start":71115,"end":71320},{"w":"Earth's","start":71320,"end":71866},{"w":"orbit.","start":71866,"end":72344}],"start":58290,"end":72344,"timing":"estimated","chunks":[0,3,7,11,18,23,27],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"NASAが資金を提供する調査プロジェクトは、ほぼ15,000の地球近傍天体-地球の軌道に周期的に近づく小惑星や彗星-の知られているカタログの98パーセントを発見した。","edge":false,"segFrom":9,"segTo":10},{"id":"s6_72344","text":"The list is growing at a rate of about 1,500 per year.","words":[{"w":"The","start":72344,"end":72618},{"w":"list","start":72618,"end":72959},{"w":"is","start":72959,"end":73164},{"w":"growing","start":73164,"end":73710},{"w":"at","start":73710,"end":73915},{"w":"a","start":73915,"end":74051},{"w":"rate","start":74051,"end":74393},{"w":"of","start":74393,"end":74598},{"w":"about","start":74598,"end":75007},{"w":"1,500","start":75007,"end":75417},{"w":"per","start":75417,"end":75690},{"w":"year.","start":75690,"end":76100}],"start":72344,"end":76100,"timing":"estimated","chunks":[0,2,4,7,10],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"そのリストは毎年約1500ずつ増えている","edge":false,"segFrom":10,"segTo":10},{"id":"s7_76100","text":"Meanwhile, researchers are giving serious thought to an even bigger problem: What would we do if a dangerous asteroid is discovered?","words":[{"w":"Meanwhile,","start":76100,"end":76880},{"w":"researchers","start":76880,"end":77731},{"w":"are","start":77731,"end":78015},{"w":"giving","start":78015,"end":78511},{"w":"serious","start":78511,"end":79078},{"w":"thought","start":79078,"end":79645},{"w":"to","start":79645,"end":79858},{"w":"an","start":79858,"end":80071},{"w":"even","start":80071,"end":80425},{"w":"bigger","start":80425,"end":80922},{"w":"problem:","start":80922,"end":81560},{"w":"What","start":81580,"end":81888},{"w":"would","start":81888,"end":82259},{"w":"we","start":82259,"end":82444},{"w":"do","start":82444,"end":82629},{"w":"if","start":82629,"end":82814},{"w":"a","start":82814,"end":82937},{"w":"dangerous","start":82937,"end":83554},{"w":"asteroid","start":83554,"end":84109},{"w":"is","start":84109,"end":84294},{"w":"discovered?","start":84294,"end":85034}],"start":76100,"end":85034,"timing":"estimated","chunks":[0,1,4,6,11,15,19],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"一方、研究者たちはもっと大きな問題について真剣に考えている：危険な小惑星が見つかったらどうすればよいのか？","edge":false,"segFrom":11,"segTo":12},{"id":"s8_85034","text":"How will we know if and when it will impact?","words":[{"w":"How","start":85034,"end":85281},{"w":"will","start":85281,"end":85589},{"w":"we","start":85589,"end":85774},{"w":"know","start":85774,"end":86083},{"w":"if","start":86083,"end":86268},{"w":"and","start":86268,"end":86515},{"w":"when","start":86515,"end":86823},{"w":"it","start":86823,"end":87008},{"w":"will","start":87008,"end":87317},{"w":"impact?","start":87317,"end":87810}],"start":85034,"end":87810,"timing":"estimated","chunks":[0,4,7],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"それはいつ地球に衝突するのか、もし衝突するのかどうか、どうやって知るのだろうか？","edge":false,"segFrom":12,"segTo":12},{"id":"s9_87830","text":"Is it possible to deflect or destroy it before it reaches Earth?","words":[{"w":"Is","start":87830,"end":88010},{"w":"it","start":88010,"end":88191},{"w":"possible","start":88191,"end":88732},{"w":"to","start":88732,"end":88913},{"w":"deflect","start":88913,"end":89394},{"w":"or","start":89394,"end":89574},{"w":"destroy","start":89574,"end":90056},{"w":"it","start":90056,"end":90236},{"w":"before","start":90236,"end":90657},{"w":"it","start":90657,"end":90838},{"w":"reaches","start":90838,"end":91319},{"w":"Earth?","start":91319,"end":91740}],"start":87830,"end":91740,"timing":"line","chunks":[0,3,7,9],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"地球に到達する前にそれをそらしたり破壊したりすることは可能か？","edge":false,"segFrom":13,"segTo":13},{"id":"s10_91760","text":"All of this work-from discovery to tracking to potential mitigation-is being done by a sprawling network of government agencies, private and public universities, and both amateur and professional astronomers.","words":[{"w":"All","start":91760,"end":92011},{"w":"of","start":92011,"end":92199},{"w":"this","start":92199,"end":92512},{"w":"work-from","start":92512,"end":93139},{"w":"discovery","start":93139,"end":93765},{"w":"to","start":93765,"end":93953},{"w":"tracking","start":93953,"end":94517},{"w":"to","start":94517,"end":94705},{"w":"potential","start":94705,"end":95332},{"w":"mitigation-is","start":95332,"end":96209},{"w":"being","start":96209,"end":96585},{"w":"done","start":96585,"end":96899},{"w":"by","start":96899,"end":97087},{"w":"a","start":97087,"end":97212},{"w":"sprawling","start":97212,"end":97839},{"w":"network","start":97839,"end":98340},{"w":"of","start":98360,"end":98541},{"w":"government","start":98541,"end":99207},{"w":"agencies,","start":99207,"end":99812},{"w":"private","start":99812,"end":100295},{"w":"and","start":100295,"end":100537},{"w":"public","start":100537,"end":100961},{"w":"universities,","start":100961,"end":101807},{"w":"and","start":101807,"end":102049},{"w":"both","start":102049,"end":102352},{"w":"amateur","start":102352,"end":102836},{"w":"and","start":102836,"end":103078},{"w":"professional","start":103078,"end":103864},{"w":"astronomers.","start":103864,"end":104650}],"start":91760,"end":104650,"timing":"line","chunks":[0,5,10,15,19,23,28],"chunksByAi":false,"ja":"このすべての作業、発見から追跡、そして潜在的な緩和まで、政府機関の広範なネットワーク、私立・公立の大学、そしてアマチュアとプロの天文学者によって行われている","edge":false,"segFrom":14,"segTo":15},{"id":"s11_104670","text":"Helping them work together is the job of NASA's Planetary Defense Coordination Office.","words":[{"w":"Helping","start":104670,"end":105143},{"w":"them","start":105143,"end":105438},{"w":"work","start":105438,"end":105733},{"w":"together","start":105733,"end":106265},{"w":"is","start":106265,"end":106442},{"w":"the","start":106442,"end":106679},{"w":"job","start":106679,"end":106915},{"w":"of","start":106915,"end":107092},{"w":"NASA's","start":107092,"end":107506},{"w":"Planetary","start":107506,"end":108097},{"w":"Defense","start":108097,"end":108569},{"w":"Coordination","start":108569,"end":109337},{"w":"Office.","start":109337,"end":109810}],"start":104670,"end":109810,"timing":"line","chunks":[0,4,7],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"彼らが協力するのを助けるのが、NASAの惑星防衛調整局の仕事だ","edge":false,"segFrom":16,"segTo":16},{"id":"s12_109830","text":"Lindley Johnson, Planetary Defense Officer at NASA Headquarters in Washington, DC says, \"Planetary Defense is a team sport.","words":[{"w":"Lindley","start":109830,"end":110369},{"w":"Johnson,","start":110369,"end":110976},{"w":"Planetary","start":110976,"end":111650},{"w":"Defense","start":111650,"end":112190},{"w":"Officer","start":112190,"end":112729},{"w":"at","start":112729,"end":112931},{"w":"NASA","start":112931,"end":113268},{"w":"Headquarters","start":113268,"end":114145},{"w":"in","start":114145,"end":114347},{"w":"Washington,","start":114347,"end":115156},{"w":"DC","start":115156,"end":115358},{"w":"says,","start":115358,"end":115763},{"w":"\"Planetary","start":115763,"end":116505},{"w":"Defense","start":116505,"end":117044},{"w":"is","start":117044,"end":117246},{"w":"a","start":117246,"end":117381},{"w":"team","start":117381,"end":117718},{"w":"sport.","start":117718,"end":118190}],"start":109830,"end":118190,"timing":"line","chunks":[0,2,5,8,11,12,14],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"NASA本部ワシントンDCの惑星防衛担当官リンドリー・ジョンソンは「惑星防衛はチームスポーツだ」と言います。","edge":false,"segFrom":17,"segTo":17},{"id":"s13_118210","text":"This office was established at NASA Headquarters to coordinate the players in planetary defense related activities across NASA, other US government agencies,","words":[{"w":"This","start":118210,"end":118495},{"w":"office","start":118495,"end":118895},{"w":"was","start":118895,"end":119123},{"w":"established","start":119123,"end":119807},{"w":"at","start":119807,"end":119978},{"w":"NASA","start":119978,"end":120264},{"w":"Headquarters","start":120264,"end":121005},{"w":"to","start":121005,"end":121176},{"w":"coordinate","start":121176,"end":121804},{"w":"the","start":121804,"end":122032},{"w":"players","start":122032,"end":122488},{"w":"in","start":122488,"end":122659},{"w":"planetary","start":122659,"end":123230},{"w":"defense","start":123230,"end":123686},{"w":"related","start":123686,"end":124143},{"w":"activities","start":124143,"end":124770},{"w":"across","start":124790,"end":125248},{"w":"NASA,","start":125248,"end":125640},{"w":"other","start":125640,"end":126033},{"w":"US","start":126033,"end":126229},{"w":"government","start":126229,"end":126948},{"w":"agencies,","start":126948,"end":127602}],"start":118210,"end":127602,"timing":"estimated","chunks":[0,2,4,7,9,11,16,18],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"この部門は、NASA内の惑星防衛関連活動を調整するために、NASA本部に設立されました。","edge":false,"segFrom":18,"segTo":19},{"id":"s14_127602","text":"and with international efforts and projects to detect any asteroid impact hazard and plan the appropriate response.\"","words":[{"w":"and","start":127602,"end":127864},{"w":"with","start":127864,"end":128191},{"w":"international","start":128191,"end":129107},{"w":"efforts","start":129107,"end":129630},{"w":"and","start":129630,"end":129891},{"w":"projects","start":129891,"end":130480},{"w":"to","start":130480,"end":130676},{"w":"detect","start":130676,"end":131134},{"w":"any","start":131134,"end":131396},{"w":"asteroid","start":131396,"end":131984},{"w":"impact","start":131984,"end":132442},{"w":"hazard","start":132442,"end":132900},{"w":"and","start":132920,"end":133214},{"w":"plan","start":133214,"end":133581},{"w":"the","start":133581,"end":133875},{"w":"appropriate","start":133875,"end":134756},{"w":"response.\"","start":134756,"end":135564}],"start":127602,"end":135564,"timing":"estimated","chunks":[0,1,4,6,8,12,14],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"そして、国際的な努力やプロジェクトと連携して、小惑星の衝突危険を検出し、適切な対応を計画します。","edge":false,"segFrom":19,"segTo":20},{"id":"s15_135564","text":"A recent real world example illustrates how this all works.","words":[{"w":"A","start":135564,"end":135711},{"w":"recent","start":135711,"end":136225},{"w":"real","start":136225,"end":136592},{"w":"world","start":136592,"end":137033},{"w":"example","start":137033,"end":137620},{"w":"illustrates","start":137620,"end":138501},{"w":"how","start":138501,"end":138795},{"w":"this","start":138795,"end":139162},{"w":"all","start":139162,"end":139456},{"w":"works.","start":139456,"end":139970}],"start":135564,"end":139970,"timing":"estimated","chunks":[0,2,5,6],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"最近の現実の例が、これがどのように機能するかを示しています。","edge":false,"segFrom":20,"segTo":20},{"id":"s16_139990","text":"Paul Chodas, manager for NASA's Center for Near Earth Object Studies at the Jet Propulsion Laboratory, describes what happened:","words":[{"w":"Paul","start":139990,"end":140296},{"w":"Chodas,","start":140296,"end":140785},{"w":"manager","start":140785,"end":141275},{"w":"for","start":141275,"end":141519},{"w":"NASA's","start":141519,"end":141948},{"w":"Center","start":141948,"end":142376},{"w":"for","start":142376,"end":142620},{"w":"Near","start":142620,"end":142926},{"w":"Earth","start":142926,"end":143293},{"w":"Object","start":143293,"end":143721},{"w":"Studies","start":143721,"end":144211},{"w":"at","start":144211,"end":144394},{"w":"the","start":144394,"end":144639},{"w":"Jet","start":144639,"end":144884},{"w":"Propulsion","start":144884,"end":145557},{"w":"Laboratory,","start":145557,"end":146291},{"w":"describes","start":146291,"end":146902},{"w":"what","start":146902,"end":147208},{"w":"happened:","start":147208,"end":147820}],"start":139990,"end":147820,"timing":"line","chunks":[0,2,3,6,11,16,17],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"ジェット推進研究所のNASA近地天体研究センター長ポール・チョダスは、何が起こったかを説明します。","edge":false,"segFrom":21,"segTo":21},{"id":"s17_147840","text":"\"The object was first detected by the NASA-funded Catalina Sky Survey near Tucson, Arizona on October 3rd, 2015 and tagged as detection WT1190F.\"","words":[{"w":"\"The","start":147840,"end":148235},{"w":"object","start":148235,"end":148787},{"w":"was","start":148787,"end":149102},{"w":"first","start":149102,"end":149576},{"w":"detected","start":149576,"end":150286},{"w":"by","start":150286,"end":150523},{"w":"the","start":150523,"end":150838},{"w":"NASA-funded","start":150838,"end":151785},{"w":"Catalina","start":151785,"end":152495},{"w":"Sky","start":152495,"end":152811},{"w":"Survey","start":152811,"end":153363},{"w":"near","start":153363,"end":153758},{"w":"Tucson,","start":153758,"end":154389},{"w":"Arizona","start":154389,"end":155020},{"w":"on","start":155020,"end":155257},{"w":"October","start":155257,"end":155888},{"w":"3rd,","start":155888,"end":156283},{"w":"2015","start":156283,"end":156677},{"w":"and","start":156677,"end":156993},{"w":"tagged","start":156993,"end":157545},{"w":"as","start":157545,"end":157782},{"w":"detection","start":157782,"end":158571},{"w":"WT1190F.\"","start":158571,"end":159360}],"start":147840,"end":159360,"timing":"line","chunks":[0,2,5,11,14,18,20],"chunksByAi":true,"ja":"その物体は、2015年10月3日にアリゾナ州ツーソン近くのNASA資金提供のカタリナ・スカイ・サーベイによって初めて検出され、検出WT1190Fとタグ付けされました。","edge":false,"segFrom":22,"segTo":22}],"segments":[{"text":"When an asteroid targeted Earth 65 million years ago, it took those masters of Earth by complete surprise.","start":23820,"dur":6850},{"text":"While we know of no large object that is on a collision course with Earth in the next 100 years,","start":30690,"dur":5190},{"text":"descendants of survivors from that catastrophic impact are determined not to make the same mistake.","start":35900,"dur":6710},{"text":"In 2016, human astronomers now routinely scan the heavens for signs of potentially hazardous objects.","start":42630,"dur":7060},{"text":"When one is discovered, alerts are issued to observers around the world so space rocks cannot easily disappear into the blackness of space.","start":49710,"dur":8560},{"text":"NASA-funded survey projects have found 98 percent of the known catalogue of almost 15,000 near-Earth objects-asteroids and comets","start":58290,"dur":7640},{"text":"whose orbits periodically bring them within 30 million miles of Earth's orbit. The list is growing at a rate of about 1,500 per year.","start":66950,"dur":10130},{"text":"Meanwhile, researchers are giving serious thought to an even bigger problem:","start":76100,"dur":5460},{"text":"What would we do if a dangerous asteroid is discovered? How will we know if and when it will impact?","start":81580,"dur":6230},{"text":"Is it possible to deflect or destroy it before it reaches Earth?","start":87830,"dur":3910},{"text":"All of this work-from discovery to tracking to potential mitigation-is being done by a sprawling network","start":91760,"dur":6580},{"text":"of government agencies, private and public universities, and both amateur and professional astronomers.","start":98360,"dur":6290},{"text":"Helping them work together is the job of NASA's Planetary Defense Coordination Office.","start":104670,"dur":5140},{"text":"Lindley Johnson, Planetary Defense Officer at NASA Headquarters in Washington, DC says, \"Planetary Defense is a team sport.","start":109830,"dur":8360},{"text":"This office was established at NASA Headquarters to coordinate the players in planetary defense related activities","start":118210,"dur":6560},{"text":"across NASA, other US government agencies, and with international efforts and projects to detect any asteroid impact hazard","start":124790,"dur":8110},{"text":"and plan the appropriate response.\" A recent real world example illustrates how this all works.","start":132920,"dur":7050},{"text":"Paul Chodas, manager for NASA's Center for Near Earth Object Studies at the Jet Propulsion Laboratory, describes what happened:","start":139990,"dur":7830},{"text":"\"The object was first detected by the NASA-funded Catalina Sky Survey near Tucson, Arizona on October 3rd, 2015 and tagged as detection WT1190F.\"","start":147840,"dur":11520}],"analysisVersion":1,"punctuatedByAi":false,"createdAt":0,"updatedAt":0,"sample":{"level":"B2","topic":"惑星防衛の解説（ScienceCasts）","reason":"一般向け科学解説。専門語と長い修飾が多いが、ナレーションは明瞭（約 145 語/分）","wpm":145,"license":"パブリックドメイン（NASA・米国政府の著作物）","credit":"NASA","sourceUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B1UQHhZHeiA"}}